<h3>My Component</h3>

<p id="e7ab04f1-1f21-4c0c-aabd-078030b87b42" class=""><strong>Exercise</strong>: In the exercises folder, create a file <code>myComponent.bx</code> which is a class. In component.bxm, make a form
    that accepts 3 numbers. Create a form on this page which accepts 3 inputs.  When the form is submitted, send the three numbers to a function in myComponent.bx and
    display the product of the three numbers on the page.</p>

<br />
<p><strong>Answer</strong>:</p>

<!---Connect to myComponent.bx file--->
<bx:set myComponent = createObject("myComponent") />

<p>Enter numbers in form below to multiply them together</p><br />
<form action="#cgi.script_name#?p=#p#" method="post">
    <div class="mb-3">
        <label for="numOne" class="form-label">First Number</label>
        <input type="number" class="form-control" id="numOne" name="first" placeholder="First Number" required>
     </div>
     <div class="mb-3">
        <label for="numTwo" class="form-label">Second Number</label>
        <input type="number" class="form-control" id="numTwo" name="second" placeholder="Second Number" required>
     </div>
    <div class="mb-3">
        <label for="numthree" class="form-label">Third Number</label>
        <input type="number" class="form-control" id="numThree" name="third" placeholder="Third Number" required>
     </div>
     <div>
        <button class="btn btn-primary">Submit</button>
     </div>
</form>

<br />

<!---Check that keys exist, and show values of each key --->
<bx:if (structKeyExists(form, "first") && structKeyExists(form, "second") && structKeyExists(form, "third"))>
   The First Number is: <bx:output>#first#</bx:output><br />
   The Second Number is: <bx:output>#second#</bx:output><br />
   The Third Number is: <bx:output>#third#</bx:output><br />

<!---Call multiplyTheNumbers function that is in the myComponent.bx file --->
   <br />
   The product of these three numbers is: <bx:output>#myComponent.multiplyTheNumbers(first,second,third)#</bx:output>
</bx:if>